centerpiece:
The Formation Gallery — the reference's measured recipe (NOTES.md 'static anatomy'), every texture ours. GEOMETRY: 32 planes, unit PlaneGeometry re-geometried to 2·aspect × 2 on texture assignment (posters 512×724, aspect 0.707 → planes 1.414 × 2 world units). MATERIAL: one shader program, cloned material per plane (per-plane uniforms, shared program); vertex = standard MVP + vUv passthrough; fragment, exact:
  vec4 tex = texture2D(uMap, vUv);
  float lum = dot(tex.rgb, vec3(0.299,0.587,0.114));
  vec3 col = mix(vec3(lum), tex.rgb, uColor);   // uColor per-plane, 0 default
  col = mix(col, uWash, 0.4);                    // whitewash, measured mix
  float fog = smoothstep(7.0, 14.0, uDist);      // OURS (pole doesn't publish range; camera z 10, formation r ≈ 6.5 → distances 3.5–16.5, so 7→14 reads as depth)
  col = mix(col, uFog, fog);
  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, tex.a * uOpacity);
transparent:true, depthWrite:false, depthTest:true. uWash = uFog = vec3(1) White / vec3(0) Night; uDist updated per plane per frame (32 uniform sets — trivial). NO lights — unlit shader, the wash is the lighting. BLENDING POLICY (measured: 'opacity fade instead of sorting'): draw order is FIXED at exhibit index — NO per-frame renderOrder churn (a draft idea, deleted: it contradicts the recipe and thrashes the renderer). Overlap conflicts are prevented by uOpacity crossfades: during any formation morph the outgoing positions' planes fade 1→0 while incoming fade 0→1 (lerp 0.05), and distant-hemisphere planes (dot(normalize(planePos−camPos), camForward) < −0.35) lerp uOpacity toward 0.25 at 0.05/frame — misordered fragments fade before they can read as errors. CAMERA: fov 45, z 10; cursor parallax ±0.4 x / ±0.25 y at lerp 0.15; camX overridden by the strip pan (v ∈ [6,7]: camX = (v−6.5)·124). FORMATIONS (per-frame position lerp 0.05 + quaternion slerp 0.05 between them): Fibonacci sphere r 6.5 — y_k = 1−2(k+0.5)/32, θ_k = k·2.399963 rad, x = r·√(1−y²)·cosθ, z = r·√(1−y²)·sinθ; jittered ring r 5.2, jitter from mulberry32(9001): Δr ±0.7, Δy ±1.1, Δθ ±4° (deterministic, never Math.random); golden-angle flower (Vogel) ρ = 1.15·√(k+1) (max ρ ≈ 6.50, scale-matched to the sphere), θ = k·137.50776°, z alternating ±0.35; cylinder r 4.2, two turns (θ = k/32·4π), y −3.8→+3.8; x-strip pos ((k−15.5)·4, 0, 0), upright. Planes billboard toward camera in formations (slerp 0.05), slerp to identity in the strip. IDLE: group yaw 0.02 rad/s in formations (one revolution per ~5 min — stillness with a pulse), frozen in strip. SCROLL: whole-page virtual scroll v ∈ [0,9] (see Frame section), wheel Δ·0.002, lerp 0.1. INTERACTION — the color reveal (our answer to the reference's Pride uniforms): raycaster against the 32 meshes from window pointer coords, only while v ∈ [0.8,7); hovered plane's uColor lerps toward 1 at 0.15/frame, all others decay toward 0 at 0.05/frame — the collection hangs grayscale until you look directly at an exhibit, then its true lab palette bleeds through the wash; identical in Night. Clicking a plane in strip mode centers it (v_target = 6.5 + (k−15.5)/31; the 0.1 lerp glides). BUDGET: 32 draw calls total (32 planes, unlit, no helpers; chrome is DOM) — under the ≤40 cap; textures 32 × 512×724 RGBA ≈ 47MB + mips ≈ 63MB, acceptable at the ≥1200px desktop-only floor; dpr = min(devicePixelRatio, 1.75); antialias true; renderer.outputColorSpace = SRGBColorSpace, texture colorSpace SRGB; render loop paused by IntersectionObserver (<15% visible) and document.hidden; renderer.setAnimationLoop with per-frame lerp only — zero per-frame allocations (positions/quaternions precomputed into Float32Arrays per formation; morphs read, never allocate).
